# Dev-only TOC, not for the client: exists purely so tests/harness.py can load the Modern
# node-conversion pass (tools/gen_modern_nodes.py) against the real engine and see what
# breaks (see Data/Modern/CONVERSION_NOTES.md for what hasn't been converted yet -- edges,
# abilities, riding skills, names -- so most of the engine's own files are left out below
# on purpose: they'd load fine, since every one of them reads its data tables defensively
# (`addon.Edges or {}` and the like), but there's nothing for them to do yet, and listing
# them here would suggest more is wired up than actually is). Not a real per-ruleset TOC;
# see docs/DESIGN.md section 1 for what that will need (Mapzeroth_Mainline.toc) once the
# data conversion is far enough along to be worth shipping.

Constants.lua
Locales.lua
Locales_UI.lua
Options.lua

